// The glossary catalogue — every entry the page shows, as data.
//
// GENERATED ONCE, FROM THE PAGE IT REPLACES, AND HAND-MAINTAINED FROM HERE ON.
// docs/ui-glossary.html used to BE this list, written as markup: 149 entries of
// hand-authored HTML that nothing could check. Extracting it verbatim is what made
// the page generable without re-authoring a single description — the prose below is
// the prose that shipped, moved rather than rewritten, because it is long, careful
// and full of history that would have been lost by starting again.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT IN ui.jsx, given the rule is 'colocate the entry with the thing'.
// Two thirds of these entries document a CSS class or a concept — .topbar, the scene
// backdrop, the material tokens — and there is no export to hang them on. The third
// that ARE components carry a `glossary` property beside the component itself, and
// glossary-registry.test.js is what makes the split safe: it fails when a component
// gains no entry, so coverage is enforced by the test rather than by which file the
// text sits in. 142KB of documentation prose inside a 295KB source file would make
// ui.jsx unreadable to buy a colocation the test already guarantees.
//
// `html` is carried markup, waiting to become a real component render. Every entry
// that names a ui.jsx export in `src` is a candidate; the count of those still on
// carried markup is asserted in the test so it can only go down.

